# openapi-generator overwrites every file it emits, and never deletes anything it does not.
# So a hand-written file only needs listing here if the generator emits something at the same
# path — otherwise it is left alone regardless. Seven entries below are load-bearing for that
# reason; the rest are defensive, and are kept so the protected set reads as one list.
# Verified by running the generator into an empty directory with no ignore file: it writes
# go.mod, go.sum, README.md, .gitignore, git_push.sh, .travis.yml and api/openapi.yaml.
#
# AGENTS.md holds the canonical enumeration, which api-codegen's generate-go-sdk.sh checks
# against. That guard matches whole lines exactly, so a variant spelling like `auth/**` still
# protects the files but fails the check.

# Authentication and client construction. The generated client has no notion of our auth
# methods, and its default server URL is empty, so this package is what makes it usable.
# Defensive: the generator emits nothing under auth/.
auth/

# The module path and dependency set are ours, not the generator's guess.
# Both load-bearing — the generator emits go.mod and go.sum.
go.mod
go.sum

# Suppressed rather than protected. openapi-generator vendors a YAML copy of its input spec
# here by default; nothing in this repo or its consumers reads it, docs/ already documents
# every operation and model, and info.version is the API's major version so the copy cannot
# identify which export produced this SDK. Keeping it would publish the internal x-mc-*
# codegen markers the input carries. Load-bearing: remove this line and the generator writes
# the file again.
api/openapi.yaml

# The root package doc comment, which is the pkg.go.dev landing page. Points at
# auth.NewClient, because NewAPIClient and NewConfiguration have no default server URL.
# Defensive: the Go generator emits no doc.go.
doc.go

# Repository documentation and tooling config, none of it generated API reference.
# README.md and .gitignore are load-bearing — the generator emits both.
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CODEOWNERS
LICENSE
SECURITY.md
.github/
.claude/
.work/
.gitignore

# The generator's own scaffolding, which we do not use. Both load-bearing: listing them is
# what keeps the generator from ever writing them, which is why neither exists in the tree.
git_push.sh
.travis.yml
